[size=4][b]World of Warcraft style combat text - bigger numbers on enemies, with a fast crit pop instead of a flat vanilla rise.[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Enemy hit numbers are 2x vanilla size. A crit is 3x, with a snap-to-peak, undershoot, settle pop rather than a smooth swell.[/*]
[*][b]Red[/b] text for an elemental weakness hit. [b]Yellow[/b] for everything else that counts as a crit: a backstab, a Valheim "Bonus" hit, or a hit at least twice the size of your recent average against that kind of enemy. Crits are also bold and clear the screen faster.[/*]
[*]The number rides up from the creature as it moves, instead of hanging in the air where the blow landed.[/*]
[*]Readable from further away - raised from vanilla's own text-visibility distance so a bow shot from range still shows a number.[/*]
[/list]

Everything else - the font, the fade, the rise speed on an ordinary hit, healing and block text - is exactly what vanilla already drew.

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]

Requires BepInEx. Unpack into your Valheim folder so the DLL lands in BepInEx/plugins. No settings to configure.

Single-player and multiplayer, client-side only. The server does not need it, and other players do not need it.

